<task id="020" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>MCP module, packages and /mcp/{area} host</title>
    <phase>B MCP host and tools</phase>
    <gate>after 003 (T0 passed; T13 route mechanism recorded)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; new module, endpoints and package changes (.cs, .csproj)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Follows existing module patterns with exact canonical references (SignalsModule, NotificationsModule:20-55, RateLimitingModule per-user partition L301-322); placement and shape are settled in design §8 B-6 and §11</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>D</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares no file with 013 (Program.cs, csproj, RateLimitingModule.cs, EndpointMappingExtensions.cs and Api/Mcp/** are not touched by 013)</parallel-reason>
    <deps>003, 017</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, minimal-api, endpoints, di, config, ai, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add the MCP host to the BFF: package ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore 2.3.1 and move Microsoft.Extensions.AI to 10.11.x with the AI regression suites green; register AddMcpModule with Mcp:Enabled (default false, null object → 503); map /mcp/{area} through MapMcpEndpoints with only legal-operations in v1, explicit RequireAuthorization, an mcp rate-limit policy per caller, a request-size limit and buffering off; and add the shared tool-result conversion.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, the ModelContextProtocol C# SDK, rate limiting and NuGet dependency management.</role>
  <goal>A stateless MCP endpoint answers at /mcp/legal-operations behind auth, rate and size limits and the kill switch; tool types are discovered per area by attribute; Api/Mcp/McpToolResults converts DecisionToolError to an isError CallToolResult; AI suites pass on Microsoft.Extensions.AI 10.11.x; the publish-size delta is recorded.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-01, NFR-04, NFR-08; design §8 B-6 and §11 (stateless, 406 trap, buffering). Phase 0 T0 and T13 results (notes/phase0-results.md) decide the route mechanism; fallback is one route that filters tools by path. Routes are /mcp/{area}; 'core' is avoided because it means core record.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Sprk.Bff.Api.csproj (add ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore 2.3.1; Microsoft.Extensions.AI and .OpenAI 10.3.0 → 10.11.x with the pinned chain at L34-L133)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/McpModule.cs (AddMcpModule; McpOptions binding; null object when disabled)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpOptions.cs (SectionName "Mcp", Enabled default false)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpEndpoints.cs (MapMcpEndpoints: /mcp/legal-operations)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpToolResults.cs (DecisionToolError → CallToolResult isError)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/RateLimitingModule.cs (add the "mcp" policy partitioned per caller, like L301-322)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Program.cs (builder.Services.AddMcpModule(builder.Configuration) beside AddSignalsModule, L110)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs (app.MapMcpEndpoints())</file>
