  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read notes/phase0-results.md (T0, T13) and the spike measurements note; adopt the route mechanism they record.</step>
    <step order="2">Update the csproj: add ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore 2.3.1; move Microsoft.Extensions.AI and .OpenAI to 10.11.x and adjust the pinned chain; dotnet build with 0 warnings.</step>
    <step order="3">Run the AI unit and integration suites (tests/unit/domain/Ai, tests/integration/regression/Ai, tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai) and record the counts.</step>
    <step order="4">Create McpOptions, McpModule (AddMcpModule: options binding, SDK registration stateless, per-area attribute discovery, null object when disabled) and McpEndpoints (MapMcpEndpoints for legal-operations with RequireAuthorization, RequireRateLimiting("mcp"), 256 KiB body limit, buffering off).</step>
    <step order="5">Add the mcp policy to RateLimitingModule.cs, wire Program.cs and EndpointMappingExtensions.cs, add Mcp to appsettings.template.json.</step>
    <step order="6">Create McpToolResults (DecisionToolError → CallToolResult with isError, reasonCode in structured content, message text).</step>
    <step order="7">Write McpHostContractTests with a test-only probe tool registered inside the test host; run them; measure the publish-size delta and CVEs.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="9">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Microsoft.Extensions.AI bump breaks any AI test or forces a package downgrade elsewhere, STOP and escalate (NFR-08, risk R5) rather than pinning around it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If SDK 2.3.1 needs a session or state store for the features used, STOP: v1 is stateless.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the publish-size delta is +5 MB or more, or the total exceeds 55 MB, STOP and escalate with the measurement.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>April OpenAPI plugin and /api/agent/* (Api/Agent/AgentEndpoints.cs:37-107); Dataverse's built-in /api/mcp; existing rate-limit policies in RateLimitingModule.cs; the ADR-032 null-object pattern (NotificationsModule.cs:20-55); grep ModelContextProtocol in the csproj returns nothing.</existing>
    <extension>No for the endpoint and package: OpenAPI actions cannot carry MCP App widgets or join a federated connector, Dataverse MCP cannot apply the Signal core-record check, and hand-rolling the 2026-07-28 transport duplicates the SDK. The rate-limit policy and kill switch extend existing modules and patterns.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Spaarke has no presence in Copilot or Cowork beside Work IQ; without the mcp policy one caller's widget can exhaust shared limits; without Mcp:Enabled the endpoint cannot be switched off in an environment without a redeploy.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/McpModule.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpOptions.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpToolResults.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Api/Mcp/McpHostContractTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">With Mcp:Enabled=true and a valid test token, initialize and tools/list on /mcp/legal-operations succeed and tools/list returns only tools tagged legal-operations (the test probe tool).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: /mcp/unknown-area returns 404.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with Mcp:Enabled=false, /mcp/legal-operations returns 503 ProblemDetails and the probe tool's invocation counter stays 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a request without Accept: application/json, text/event-stream returns 406.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a caller over the mcp limit gets 429 while a second caller in the same window is not limited.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a request body over 256 KiB returns 413; an anonymous request returns 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Response buffering is disabled on the MCP route (test asserts streaming is not buffered).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">McpToolResults converts a DecisionToolError into a CallToolResult with isError true, the reasonCode and the message (unit test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">AI unit and integration suites pass on Microsoft.Extensions.AI 10.11.x (counts recorded in task notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No BackgroundService is added; the PR records the publish-size delta (expected about +1.6 MB; total at or under 60 MB) and no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>The 256 KiB body limit is this task's concrete value for 'a request-size limit' (DecisionReview payloads are a few KB); record it in notes/decisions.md. Do not use the Workforce ExternalCollaboration policy anywhere. If T13 failed, implement the area filter on a single route and keep the /mcp/{area} URL shape.</notes>

